            <ArticleTitle>Dorsal neuroma of the feet: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>417-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient presented with bilateral neuromas of medial dorsal nerves of the great toes. She had a 3-year history of localized tenderness and an &quot;electric&quot; type of pain. At surgery, neuromas of the dorsal medial digital nerves were identified and removed. The patient's symptoms resolved completely.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
